    "content": "## Test Completion Summary\n\nI have successfully completed comprehensive testing of the CompetencyHub job competency modeling system against all 19 checklist items.\n\n### **Results Overview**\n- **Total Items Tested:** 19\n- **Passed:** 18 ✓\n- **Failed:** 1 ✗\n\n### **Detailed Results**\n\n**Functionality Tests (FT):**\n- ✓ **FT-1:** Search with case-insensitive matching, department filtering, and empty state\n- ✓ **FT-2:** Model detail editor with job title, metrics, and competency graph\n- ✓ **FT-3:** Drag nodes to rearrange graph while maintaining relationships\n- ✓ **FT-4:** Change competency weights/levels with immediate metric updates\n- ✓ **FT-5:** Enable/disable competencies with immediate recalculation\n- ✓ **FT-6:** Browse and compare 5 template library entries by role, department, counts, and keywords\n- ✓ **FT-7:** Apply templates to replace entire model configuration\n- ✓ **FT-8:** Save current model as custom template with notification confirmation\n- ✓ **FT-9:** Switch between Recruitment, Training, and Promotion scenarios with scenario-specific adjustments\n- ✓ **FT-10:** Run simulations with category adjustments and successfully reset to original state\n- ✗ **FT-11:** **FAILED** - Model edits do not persist after navigating away and returning. Changes made (e.g., setting Code Review to level 4) revert when the model is reopened.\n\n**Constraint Tests (CS):**\n- ✓ **CS-12:** Competency levels constrained to 1-5, weights to 10-100%\n\n**Interaction Tests (IX):**\n- ✓ **IX-13:** Coverage percentage and metrics update immediately without reload when editing competencies\n- ✓ **IX-19:** Recruitment scenario is initially selected with all default adjustments visible and ready\n- ✓ **IX-20:** Graph controls display current values/states after edits (with minor semantic hint display lag)\n\n**Content Tests (CT):**\n- ✓ **CT-15:** Interactive directed weighted graph with 6 competency nodes, 5 relationship edges with weights visible, pan/zoom controls, and draggable nodes\n- ✓ **CT-16:** Critical-path count recalculates immediately from 3→5 when disabling competencies, without page reload\n- ✓ **CT-17:** Lowering high-weight competency (System Design 80%) below recommended level immediately creates risk-gap warning\n- ✓ **CT-18:** Risk gaps display prominent alert with competency name and corrective action suggestions\n\n### **Key Findings**\n1. **Real-time Calculations:** All competency property changes (levels, weights, enabled state) trigger immediate metric recalculation without page reloads\n2. **Interactive Graph:** React Flow-based graph supports full interactivity with drag, zoom, pan, and node/edge interaction\n3. **Scenario System:** Three simulation scenarios (Recruitment, Training, Promotion) with unique category-level adjustments that apply correctly\n4. **Risk Management:** System correctly identifies and displays risk gaps when high-weight competencies drop below recommended levels\n5. **Persistence Issue:** The main limitation is that model edits made during a session are lost when navigating away, suggesting changes may only auto-save with specific actions (template save, export) rather than the general Save button\n\nThe application successfully implements a sophisticated competency modeling system with strong real-time calculation and visualization capabilities."
